    "risk_matrix": {
      "as_of": "2026-07-16T22:24:11.455298+00:00",
      "model": "claude-sonnet-5",
      "provenance": "reviewed_artifact",
      "rows": [
        {
          "dimension": "Smart-contract",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Yearn's own V3 vault line has been audited by ChainSecurity and MixBytes and carries no disclosed exploit of its own. The 2021 incident hit an early V1 DAI vault and was largely contained — Yearn's security team recovered 24 of 35M DAI within roughly 11 minutes. The 2025 yETH exploit hit a standalone weighted-stableswap AMM codebase, built and maintained separately from the V3 vault line with its own team and structure, not the audited vaults product itself. The clearest residual exposure is third-party strategies deployed permissionlessly through Yearn's V3 factory outside Yearn's own curated, role-gated, internally-reviewed vaults. Yearn also created the first DeFi security program, yAcademy — now the yAudit security-review practice — an in-house auditing capability few protocols maintain.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Governance",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Ongoing tokenomics debates — shifting from vote-escrow to vote-lock, oYFI buybacks, and yLockers — indicate governance is active but unsettled, creating execution risk.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Liquidity",
          "level": "Medium-Low",
          "note": "The large majority of Yearn's TVL — V3 vaults and yvUSD — is redeemable on demand, subject to ordinary strategy liquidity buffers, and there has been no depeg event. yCRV's discount to CRV is a structural, permanent feature of a max-locked, non-unwrappable CRV position; Yearn's own documentation describes this discount as normal and expected for a locked-CRV wrapper, not a liquidity failure, and it is scoped to that one wrapper product rather than the bulk of TVL.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Market",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "The $9M dYdX insurance fund loss from alleged YFI market manipulation shows that thin YFI liquidity makes the token susceptible to coordinated price attacks.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Centralization",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Yearn operates with a small, informally structured contributor base; governance and security processes (peer review, security-team review, YIP votes) are structural rather than resting on any single named individual. Contributor-pool expansion via subDAOs (e.g. Resupply), yLockers, and the Builders Collective broadens participation but has not yet been paired with clear on-chain enforcement of contributor authority or succession.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Regulatory",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Andre Cronje's stated reason for his 2022 exit was regulatory caution, and Yearn's yield products spanning multiple chains attract ongoing scrutiny as potential unregistered securities.",
          "source": ""
        }
      ],
      "sourced": 0,
      "total": 6
    },
